#files made - .gitignore , .git(hidden folder) , readme.md , .gitattributes , LICENSE

# It depends on what pattern you put in .gitignore.

# Case 1: Ignore a specific folder
# PrivateNotes/
# This ignores the folder named PrivateNotes only in the repository root.
# Example:
# Vault/
# ├── PrivateNotes/      ← Ignored
# ├── Projects/
# │   └── PrivateNotes/  ← NOT ignored

# Case 2: Ignore a folder name anywhere
# **/PrivateNotes/
# or simply
# PrivateNotes
# This ignores every folder or file named PrivateNotes anywhere in the vault.
# Example:
# Vault/
# ├── PrivateNotes/          ← Ignored
# ├── Projects/
# │   └── PrivateNotes/      ← Ignored
# ├── Notes/
# │   └── PrivateNotes/      ← Ignored

# Case 3: Ignore a specific path
# Projects/Secrets/
# Only this folder is ignored:
# Vault/
# ├── Projects/
# │   └── Secrets/      ← Ignored
# ├── Notes/
# │   └── Secrets/      ← NOT ignored